  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "image-overlay-card",
      "data": {
        "title": "About the Department",
        "bgImg": "/images/kce/academics/cyber-security/cybersecurity-web-image.png",
        "description": [
          "<p>The Department was established in 2020 with an Undergraduate Programme in Computer Science and Engineering (Cyber Security). The programme is thoughtfully designed to develop essential Graduate Attributes, equipping students to pursue diverse and dynamic career paths such as Cyber Security Analyst, Penetration Tester (Ethical Hacker), Cloud Security Engineer, Security Architect, and other emerging roles aligned with the evolving demands of the global job market.</p><p>The curriculum is continuously enhanced through inputs from industry experts, ensuring that students remain up to date with the latest trends, tools, and best practices in the rapidly advancing field of cybersecurity. It offers a balanced integration of strong theoretical foundations and practical, hands-on learning across key domains including Ethical Hacking, Cryptography, Cyber Forensics, Vulnerability Assessment, Network Security, and Secure Software Development.</p>"
        ]
      }
    },

    {
      "type": "plain-para",
      "data": {
        "content": [
          "Students also benefit from experiential learning in state-of-the-art laboratories, gaining proficiency in advanced tools and techniques, including those offered by globally recognized organizations such as EC-Council.",
          "The department has well-experienced and highly-motivated faculty members and their major areas include Networking and network Security, Ethical hacking, Web Application Security, Penetration Testing, Malware analysis and Cyber Forensics. The faculty members impart their knowledge and skills to the students to achieve the goals of the department.",
          "The faculty members are encouraged to publish articles in national and international journals. The Department has signed MoUs with leading industries and organizations for establishing collaborative research, conducting Workshops, Seminars and for organizing International Conferences. Professional association CyberWatch Center is developed for professional interaction."
        ]
      }
    },
